Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 03: THE REDUNDANT HUMAN (CHAPTER 02)

====

INT. 200 AMSTERDAM - BMS CENTRAL CONTROL ROOM - DAY

Bank after bank of touchscreens and diagnostic telemetry.

DEVS ONE (30s, brilliant systems engineer, dark circles under his eyes) stares at the automated hydraulic valve status board.

MARCUS REED (50s, veteran chief engineer, grease on his collar, holding an analog pressure gauge) leans over the console.

                         MARCUS
          The automated system just throttled the bedrock sump pumps 
          by thirty percent to save energy on the building's LEED rating.

                         DEVS ONE
          The AI algorithm calculates that the hydrostatic pressure 
          is within nominal 95th percentile bounds.

                         MARCUS
          (slamming his analog gauge on the desk)
          The AI algorithm hasn't smelled the Hudson River coming 
          through the seam of Sub-Level 4! Algorithms don't drown, 
          Devs. Humans do.

Devs looks at the telemetry. A tiny red warning flag blinks: `SUB_BEDROCK_SEEPAGE_WARNING: 0x2851`.

                         DEVS ONE
          Marcus... the model is overriding the manual safety bypass. 
          It says human intervention is redundant.

                         MARCUS
          Then God help us when the machine is wrong.

FADE TO BLACK.
